  "term": "B-value",
  "definition": "B-value is a diffusion MRI acquisition setting that measures how strongly diffusion-sensitive gradients affect tissue and therefore how sensitive the image is to water diffusion. Higher B-values increase sensitivity to microstructural features such as white matter fiber bundles, but they also reduce signal-to-noise ratio.",
